{"type":"text","timestamp":1787389653987,"sessionID":"ses_fd74755c0ffedgzFACNfnreJi4","part":{"id":"prt_028b9ab5d001rSmsrEy2ZfaWB8","messageID":"msg_028b99fc4001U8AtTUr6li9OnU","sessionID":"ses_fd74755c0ffedgzFACNfnreJi4","type":"text","text":"The interface is fully preserved and no other code relies on behavior I changed. The refactor is complete.\n\nSummary of the change to `internal/lrucache.js`:\n- `get(key)` now moves the entry to the most-recently-used position (delete + re-`set`).\n- `set(key, value)` updates recency on existing keys and evicts the LRU entry (first `Map` key) whenever `size > max`, so it never exceeds `max`.\n- `set` still returns `this` and skips storing `undefined`.\n- `delete(key)` still returns whether the key was present.\n\nVerified the LRU eviction order directly, and that parsing 5000 distinct ranges (forcing eviction with the default `max` of 1000) still yields correct, deterministic results. The failing `range.test.js` cases are pre-existing and unrelated to the cache.","time":{"start":1787389651805,"end":1787389653984}}}
